the principle of least privilege is  fairly straightforward  every user should only be granted the  permission they need only when they need  them  implementing this principle however can  be complex  and then add in the need to scale at a  pace of a growing cloud  in today's video we're diving into iam  recommender a google cloud tool that  makes implementing least privilege and  securing your cloud easier  following the principle of least  privilege is one of the core tenets of  maintaining a strong security posture  unfortunately as cloud practitioners we  don't implement this practice enough  according to gartner research by 2023 99  of security failures will be the cloud  customers fault  why is that  well enforcing this privilege can be  complex and labor-intensive  first you need to understand each user  permissions they have and which ones  they need for their day-to-day work  next you need to identify which  permissions each user is likely to need  in the future so that you minimize the  toil of incremental updates  then you need to translate these  requirements into iim policies and roles  finally you need to establish processes  to regularly re-evaluate these policies  remove excess permissions and monitor  their use closely  oh and since the cloud is built to scale  this overall process needs to scale as  well iam recommender is a tool that  eases enforcing leads privilege by  helping automate steps and making it  possible to manage them efficiently at  scale  how does it work  iam recommender creates daily policy  recommendations and serves them to you  automatically  it does this by looking back at the  permission usage over the last 90 days  and finding used and unused permissions  next a machine learning model looks at  the use permissions and determines  inferred permissions  these are permissions that have been  granted but not yet used however we can  predict that they will likely be needed  in the future based on similar usage  patterns observed elsewhere  iam recommender then uses this  information to recommend a new role that  removes unused permissions and keeps  inferred permissions  the best part  no configuration or setup is required  google cloud stores a log data that  supports its functionality and there is  no charge to you  let's head into the cloud console and  see recommender in action  recommender is built directly into the  im page  where it shows you the permissions you  have given and how many are actually  being used  again there is no need to collect and  parse through activity logs we've done  all that hard work for you  in our example project you can see that  there are some users using very few  permissions that they've been granted  a light bulb icon indicates where  recommenders ml models have determined a  better fitting role  click in to get more details about the  recommended role and which permissions  will be removed or added  you can take action and apply the change  by clicking the apply button if  recommender identifies a common  permission usage pattern that does not  map to an existing role it may suggest  creating a new project level custom role  in this case you can customize the  recommendation adding or removing a  specific permission before you apply the  changes this customization action also  helps continually train the ml model for  future recommendations  over on the recommendations history tab  you can see all the recommendations you  have applied and revert them if needed  it also tracks your progress towards  least privilege  another area of the console is the  recommender hub this gives another view  of your iam recommendations as well as  the option to export them to bigquery so  that you can perform custom analysis  across your organization  in addition to retrieving  recommendations in the console you can  also use the recommender api or the  google cloud cli gcloud command now  you're ready to use iam recommender to  help strengthen security of your  deployment  it gives you back time by helping  automate and bringing ml powered  intelligence to the process of enforcing  least privilege to learn more about im  recommender and the other tools that are  part of the policy intelligence toolbox  check out cloud.google.com slash policy  intelligence
 

